paths: file:v3/src/Lower.scala file:specs/ssc3-extensions.md file:v3/extension-gate.sh file:BUGS.md file:v3/SPRINT.md file:v3/src/Parser.scala file:v3/src/Ast.scala
scope: |
  `extension` is REFUSED in Parser.scala today; the feature needs the parser to accept a
  declaration, the AST to carry it and Lower to lift each def to a top-level function whose
  first parameter is the receiver, plus a call-site rewrite. §51 records a reverted attempt
  (N 188 -> 130, CRASH 0 -> 131) and its lesson: a bare name-based rewrite catches `.map` on a
  list. The conservative form is sound in one direction — rewrite only when the name is neither
  a built-in method nor declared by any class in the merged program — and the built-in
  vocabulary is kept honest by a gate that derives it from Exec rather than by a hand list.
next: plan the task into SPRINT.md, then implement
